tools.description:
Retrieve a comment by ID

Returns a single comment identified by its unique ID. Use this endpoint to fetch the full content and metadata of a specific comment.

HTTP GET /comments/{comment_id}

Update a comment

Replaces the body of an existing comment. Only the comment author or a project admin can update a comment. Returns the updated comment object.

HTTP PUT /comments/{comment_id}

Delete a comment

Permanently removes a comment. Only the comment author or a project admin can delete a comment. This action cannot be undone.

HTTP DELETE /comments/{comment_id}

Retrieve a project by ID

Returns a single project identified by its unique ID. Use this endpoint to fetch full project details including status and timestamps.

HTTP GET /projects/{project_id}

Update a project

Updates the name or description of an existing project. Only project owners and admins can update projects. Returns the updated project object.

HTTP PUT /projects/{project_id}

Delete a project

Permanently deletes a project and all associated tasks, comments, and tag assignments. This action cannot be undone. Only the project owner can delete a project.

HTTP DELETE /projects/{project_id}

Retrieve a tag by ID

Returns a single tag identified by its unique ID. Use this endpoint to fetch the full details of a specific tag.

HTTP GET /tags/{tag_id}

Update a tag

Updates the name or color of an existing tag. Changes propagate to all tasks that use this tag. Returns the updated tag object.

HTTP PUT /tags/{tag_id}

Delete a tag

Permanently removes a tag and detaches it from all tasks. This action cannot be undone. Tasks previously tagged retain their other tags.

HTTP DELETE /tags/{tag_id}

Retrieve a task by ID

Returns a single task identified by its unique ID. Use this endpoint to fetch full task details including status, assignee, and timestamps.

HTTP GET /tasks/{task_id}

Update a task

Updates the title, description, status, or assignee of an existing task. Only project members can update tasks. Returns the updated task object.

HTTP PUT /tasks/{task_id}

Delete a task

Permanently deletes a task and all its comments. This action cannot be undone. Tag assignments are also removed. Only the task creator or a project admin can delete a task.

HTTP DELETE /tasks/{task_id}

Attach a tag to a task

Associates a tag with the specified task. If the tag is already attached, the operation is idempotent and returns the current state. A task can have multiple tags.

HTTP PUT /tasks/{task_id}/tags/{tag_id}

Detach a tag from a task

Removes the association between a tag and the specified task. The tag itself is not deleted and remains available for other tasks.

HTTP DELETE /tasks/{task_id}/tags/{tag_id}

Retrieve a user by ID

Returns a single user profile identified by its unique ID. Use this endpoint to look up team member details for task assignment or collaboration.

HTTP GET /users/{user_id}

Update a user profile

Updates the display name or role of an existing user. Only workspace admins can change roles. Users can update their own display name. Returns the updated user object.

HTTP PUT /users/{user_id}
